   "type": "text",
   "content": "The average transmittance of the films increased as the increases of the  $ O_{2} $ partial flow rates from 0 to 3sccm in the Ar sputtering atmosphere, changing from approximately 86.5% to 95% within the visible range (table 1 and figure 5). The absorption edges obviously shifted towards large band gaps as the increases of the oxygen flows up to 2sccm, showed in the inner graph in figure 5. Then the band gap of the film decreased again when the oxygen flow rate increased to 3sccm. In optical theory of thin films, the total incident light to be 1, then",
   "raw_label": "text",
   "raw_backend_id": "3",
   "confidence": null
  },
